#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079251} :activity/id #uuid "e7f6f017-93f9-5ce1-878c-ac54092f9307" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050928 :topic/id #uuid "72768bc7-3788-5996-b850-882ff2ef4f6b" :topic/math-academy-id 611} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079251 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079643 :tutorial/content "The reciprocals of sine, cosine, and tangent are given special names:\n\n- The reciprocal of **sine** is **cosecant**, abbreviated $\\csc.$\n\n$$\n\\csc(\\theta) = \\dfrac 1 {\\sin(\\theta)} = \\dfrac 1 {\\dfrac {\\text{opposite}} {\\text{hypotenuse}}} = \\dfrac {\\text{hypotenuse}} {\\text{opposite}}\n$$\n\n- The reciprocal of **cosine** is **secant**, abbreviated $\\sec.$\n\n$$\n\\sec (\\theta) = \\dfrac 1 {\\cos(\\theta)} = \\dfrac 1 {\\dfrac {\\text{adjacent}} {\\text{hypotenuse}}} = \\dfrac {\\text{hypotenuse}} {\\text{adjacent}}\n$$\n\n- The reciprocal of **tangent** is **cotangent**, abbreviated $\\cot.$\n\n$$\n\\cot (\\theta) = \\dfrac 1 {\\tan(\\theta)} = \\dfrac 1 {\\dfrac {\\text{opposite}} {\\text{adjacent}}} = \\dfrac {\\text{adjacent}} {\\text{opposite}}\n$$\n\nLet's write down expressions for $\\csc(B),$ $\\sec(B),$ and $\\cot(B)$ for the triangle below.\n\n![](images/e9/e98dcc332739ff381e8dc43160a907e471062c5b8a75567ba7dbb8687c008efa.png)\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\csc(B) &= \\dfrac {\\text{hypotenuse}} {\\text{opposite}} = \\dfrac c b \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\sec(B) &= \\dfrac {\\text{hypotenuse}} {\\text{adjacent}} = \\dfrac c a \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\cot(B) &= \\dfrac {\\text{adjacent}} {\\text{opposite}} = \\dfrac a b \\\n\t}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "4c546565-505e-5036-a606-7fec250d5073" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2453 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "52fa6b29-a997-555b-b6a1-660efa77d5b2" :step/math-academy-id 10986 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079252}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079252 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078398 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078264 :question/id #uuid "4f967310-913e-5082-ab9b-87b1eceb3ddb" :question/math-academy-id "e-3258"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e360e71d-82f6-5226-af82-bfc4d0e5363d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049915}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078950} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078951} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540049} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540101} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557237} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557269} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557284}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratios Given a Triangle"} :step/id #uuid "9b0bf911-fcdf-579f-8c6c-66de2c729bc8" :step/math-academy-id 10987 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079253}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079253 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079644 :tutorial/content "If we are given two sides of a right triangle, how can we calculate the reciprocal ratios $\\sec,$ $\\csc,$ or $\\cot$ when we are missing one of the necessary sides in the ratio?\n\nThe trick here is the same that we use for finding $\\sin,$ $\\cos,$ or $\\tan\\mathbin{:}$ we use the Pythagorean theorem for finding the missing side.\n\nTo illustrate, let's calculate $\\csc L$  in the triangle below. \n\n![](images/9f/9f2e4ea4922783c84a6cb59c5e1532b726d46c9a837a5b1eaa203bbdc6cc1741.png)\n\nRemember that $\\csc$ is the reciprocal of $\\sin.$ So first we need to compute sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin L = \\dfrac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} = \\dfrac{JK}{KL} = \\dfrac{JK}{4}\n$$\n\nTo find the length $JK,$ we can use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}JK & =\\sqrt{K{L}^{2}-J{L}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}-{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16-9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\sin L = \\dfrac{JK}{4} = \\dfrac{ \\sqrt{7} }{4},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡L & ={(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot \\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{7}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "c27dd2eb-7f81-577d-805d-4dae042300e6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2455 :tutorial/title "The Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratios and the Pythagorean Theorem"} :step/id #uuid "bd643db6-23eb-5063-a803-0b486a1997c2" :step/math-academy-id 10990 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079254}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079254 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078399 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078265 :question/id #uuid "d2f40096-4001-5cd9-aeda-52c5894649b4" :question/math-academy-id "e-3261"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8659f97-a242-543f-9668-f547ca1f4d95" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048299}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079029} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079037} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540062} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540074}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratio Given a Triangle Using the Pythagorean Theorem"} :step/id #uuid "136b4b27-154f-533e-84ed-203765c9ca7f" :step/math-academy-id 10991}] :activity/title "The Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratios" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186078641}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557368} :activity/id #uuid "e4654e7e-0783-5c4b-a381-592a4804452d" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050928 :topic/id #uuid "72768bc7-3788-5996-b850-882ff2ef4f6b" :topic/math-academy-id 611} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557336 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557284 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06980bfe-f4c2-59c0-8db4-500d4f600965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{101}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556445} {:answer/id #uuid "87680cff-ca5e-5791-b7fd-173d0bc12c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{99}{101}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556748} {:answer/id #uuid "9d14e644-7bec-5504-bb18-536fcfc2c58c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{101}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556812} {:answer/id #uuid "e146595e-4dd8-5691-b868-4d63b02ddb93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{99}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556987} {:answer/id #uuid "e6801668-fda8-53a4-a4f5-f1763efffefd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{99}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556999}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556445} :answer-field/id #uuid "b356e06c-c772-5d04-9547-6cc9819c8611" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9776a674-b453-514c-8110-e6416b1678fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-25071" :question/problem "![](images/18/184605ecccca3547b5535ef5783f93fd5e9a65e3367b601eb14fa84962da2972.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{csc}⁡C=$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the cosecant of the angle $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡C=\\frac{\\text{hypotenuse}}{\\text{opposite}}=\\frac{101}{20}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "03e32401-df3c-5835-ab23-3c8cb7d34eca"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557351 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557269 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "367e23e2-93e0-5909-a96d-94ffc82ea0a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556548} {:answer/id #uuid "7b425601-205d-5df4-afa0-eb78a4306207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556716} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad3b46b-8d3a-576a-9535-82f765e62818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556761} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b443db-abcb-5cee-8255-d1d9c8ceb1c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556891} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0d6268-11f7-5d6e-bdcb-bae4d25a0475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556922}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556761} :answer-field/id #uuid "523862e1-375c-585e-b0c5-460919f499f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "76554d51-a4eb-517f-a2a7-3724b0e31c74" :question/math-academy-id "q-25057" :question/problem "In the right triangle $GHI,$ $∠G$ is a right angle, $GH=24,$ $HI=26$ and $GI=10.$ What is the value of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡I?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's draw the triangle.\n\n![](images/14/1429b33d88f438268a4168f57ff1417586c74e2dd034ff6241e0d2fddb6146b2.png)\n\nWe compute the cosecant of the angle $I$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡I=\\frac{\\text{hypotenuse}}{\\text{opposite}}=\\frac{26}{24}=\\frac{13}{12}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3845ff3b-fd6a-5233-99ae-c7ac1028703e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557336}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557368 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1749d577-c08c-5c07-ac2a-8620c8f2e14f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556480} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa8cfc2-0abf-5a0b-ae9e-9efe4d455d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556572} {:answer/id #uuid "640901bf-75f6-5b42-80f0-a7333a046e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556658} {:answer/id #uuid "a5e1e2d9-43a9-5795-a935-fe772485a09e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556834} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ec60fa-3bd8-5560-bf34-4d082ebbd5b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557047}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556658} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d0fb2e1-70a1-53cb-877d-cddbf3ba7cdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3cfa23a7-bca9-5408-b04d-471de7fe17c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-4640" :question/problem "![](images/1c/1c6079401f61658b450e105b113bea6e979040dbdcdd53a954479809480c2c03.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{csc}⁡B=$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the cosecant of the angle $B$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡B=\\frac{\\text{hypotenuse}}{\\text{opposite}}=\\frac{17}{8}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "75809ab1-ca36-5e2b-a707-ec10935a2237" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557351}}] :activity/title "The Reciprocal Trigonometric Ratios" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556423}]}
